    "math_academy_id": "q-84066",
    "knowledge_point_id": "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700",
    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable",
    "problem": "A stack of cards has $8$ cards labeled with three and $4$ cards labeled with six. If one card is randomly drawn from the stack,  what is its expected value?",
    "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S={3,6}.$\n\nIn the stack there are $8$ cards labeled with three and $4$ cards labeled with six (twelve cards in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3) & =\\frac{8}{12}=\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ P(6) & =\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =3\\cdot f(3)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{2}{3})+6(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
